================================================================
OSI Model (7 Layers)
================================================================
Mnemonic: All People Seem To Need Data Processing
(Top → Bottom)



================================================================
7. Application
================================================================

👉 What users & applications interact with

Examples: HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP, DNS

This is where your browser, curl, Postman live

Deals with requests, responses, APIs

🔹 If a website isn’t loading → start thinking here


================================================================
6. Presentation
================================================================
👉 Data formatting, encryption, compression

Examples:

SSL/TLS encryption

JSON ↔ XML ↔ binary

Makes sure data is readable by the application

🔹 HTTPS encryption happens here

================================================================
5. Session
================================================================
👉 Session management

Establishes, maintains, terminates sessions

Authentication sessions, checkpoints, re-connects

🔹 “Are we still connected?” layer


================================================================
4. Transport
================================================================

👉 End-to-end communication & reliability

Protocols: TCP, UDP

Handles:

Ports (80, 443, 5432)

Flow control

Retransmission

🔹 TCP handshake (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK) happens here

================================================================
3. Network
================================================================

👉 Routing & IP addressing

Protocols: IP, ICMP

Devices: Routers

Decides best path to destination

🔹 ping, traceroute → Layer 3


================================================================
2. Data Link
================================================================

👉 MAC addresses & local delivery

Ethernet, ARP

Devices: Switches

Frames data for physical transmission

🔹 ARP: “Who has this IP? Tell me your MAC”

================================================================
1. Physical
================================================================
👉 Actual bits on the wire

Cables, fiber, voltages, NICs

0s and 1s

🔹 Broken cable = Layer 1 issue


================================================================
Quick DevOps / Troubleshooting Mapping
================================================================
Problem	Likely Layer
Cable unplugged	Layer 1
ARP not resolving	Layer 2
No route to host	Layer 3
Port blocked / firewall	Layer 4
Session drops	Layer 5
SSL cert error	Layer 6
500 / API error	Layer 7


================================================================
Real-World Example: Accessing a Website
================================================================
Layer 7 – Browser sends HTTP request

Layer 6 – Encrypts using TLS

Layer 5 – Session established

Layer 4 – TCP ensures delivery

Layer 3 – IP routing

Layer 2 – MAC resolution

Layer 1 – Bits sent over cable



| OSI Layer | Name         | Example Protocols     |
| --------- | ------------ | --------------------- |
| 7         | Application  | HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, DNS |
| 6         | Presentation | SSL/TLS               |
| 5         | Session      | NetBIOS, RPC          |
| 4         | Transport    | TCP, UDP              |
| 3         | Network      | IP, ICMP              |
| 2         | Data Link    | Ethernet, ARP         |
| 1         | Physical     | Cables, signals       |




===============================================
OSI Layers – How They Work (Real Example)
===============================================

🎯 Scenario

You open a browser and access:

https://www.example.com

===============================================
7️⃣ Application Layer
===============================================

👉 What you do

You type the URL
Browser creates an HTTP GET request
Protocols involved
HTTP / HTTPS
DNS (to resolve domain)
📌 This is where applications live

===============================================
6️⃣ Presentation Layer
===============================================

👉 Data preparation

HTTP data is encrypted using TLS
Data is formatted (JSON, HTML, etc.)
📌 This ensures secure & readable data

===============================================
5️⃣ Session Layer
===============================================

👉 Session management

TLS session is created
Keeps the session alive
Handles reconnects if needed
📌 “Are we still connected?”

===============================================
4️⃣ Transport Layer
===============================================

👉 Reliable delivery

TCP connection is created
3-way handshake happens
SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK
Data split into segments
Port used: 443
📌 Ensures data reaches correctly

===============================================
3️⃣ Network Layer
===============================================

👉 Routing

Source IP & destination IP added
Router decides the best path
📌 Moves packet across networks

===============================================
2️⃣ Data Link Layer
===============================================

👉 Local delivery

Converts IP → MAC using ARP
Frames created
Switches forward frames
📌 Delivers within local network

===============================================
1️⃣ Physical Layer
===============================================

👉 Transmission

Bits (0s & 1s) sent over:
Ethernet
Fiber
Wi-Fi
📌 Actual electrical / optical signals

===============================================
🔁 On the Server Side
===============================================
The process happens in reverse order:
1️⃣ → 7️⃣
Server reads bits → frames → packets → segments → decrypted → HTTP response sent back

===============================================
Short Summary
===============================================
When a user accesses a website, the request is created at the application layer, encrypted at the presentation layer, managed by the session layer, reliably transmitted by TCP at the transport layer, routed by IP at the network layer, framed using MAC at the data link layer, and finally transmitted as bits at the physical layer.


==============================================================================================
If ping works but website doesn’t, which layer is broken?
==============================================================================================
A:

Ping → Layer 3 works
Website → Layer 4 or 7 issue
